<tr><td>53</td><td><span class="evidence-tag">Audiovisual input</span></td><td>Webb, S., &amp; Rodgers, M. P. H. (2009). The lexical coverage of movies. Applied Linguistics, 30(3), 407–427.</td><td>Movies also demand high lexical coverage; imagery can aid inference, but unknown-word density can still overwhelm comprehension for lower-proficiency learners.</td></tr>
